y\" feel that limits reply rates."},{id:"control-links",question:"Can users control when links are sent?",answer:"Yes. You can edit reply coaching in Manage Ava > Autonomous replies. You set the campaign logic, messaging, and timing. Ava handles the execution based on your rules."},{id:"prospect-delays",question:"What happens if a prospect delays?",answer:"If a prospect shows interest but doesn't book right away, Ava keeps the conversation going. If they go quiet, Ava adjusts her approach rather than sending the same message again. Ava uses context from previous messages to keep things relevant and follows up multiple times until the lead shows negative intent or replies."},{id:"follow-up-prospects",question:"How does Ava follow up with prospects?",answer:"Ava runs multi-step sequences across email and social media. Each follow-up is personalized using the data Ava has gathered on the prospect, including firmographic, technographic, and intent signals. She self-optimizes over time based on what's actually driving positive replies for your campaigns, so follow-ups get better the longer she runs."},{id:"calendars-supported",question:"Which calendars are supported?",answer:"Artisan integrates with Google Calendar and Microsoft Outlook. Booked meetings show up directly on your team's calendars with no manual entry required."},{id:"different-from-scheduling",question:"How is it different from traditional meeting scheduling software?",answer:"Traditional scheduling tools like Calendly handle one step: letting someone pick a time once they're already interested. They don't find the prospect, write the outreach, run the follow-up sequences, or detect when someone is ready to book. Ava handles the full pipeline, from lead discovery and personalized outreach to reply management and getting the meeting on your calendar."}];var i=e.i(76452);e.i(25807);var l=e.i(4551),n=e.i(89493),r=e.i(73208),d=e.i(34565);let c=()=>(0,t.jsx)("section",{className:"relative overflow-hidden rounde